message: >-
  If you use this software or its bundled research evidence, please cite it
  using this metadata and identify the Git commit used.
type: software
title: >-
  InverPINN: Diagnosing Source-Strength Bias in Physics-Informed Neural
  Networks for Sparse Pollution Source Inversion
# The sole name supported by the repository's Git authorship metadata.
authors:
  - given-names: Hadis
# Existing package version; no release tag or publication date is implied.
version: 0.0.0
abstract: >-
  Controlled synthetic research on sparse single-source inversion with
  physics-informed neural networks and classical PDE-constrained inversion.
  Final J1 confirmation failed: 23 of 30 recoveries, with 27 required;
  classical inversion recovered 30 of 30 on identical observations.
keywords:
  - inverse problems
  - physics-informed neural networks
  - advection-diffusion
  - source-strength bias
